# TOEFL Reading Day54

## Topic: Animal Communication

Animals use various signals to communicate with members of their own species. These signals may include sounds, body movements, colors, and chemical substances. Communication helps animals find mates, warn others of danger, and protect their territories.

Some signals are relatively simple, while others involve complex patterns. For example, certain birds produce different calls depending on the type of threat they detect. These calls can provide information about the location or behavior of a predator.

However, animal communication is not always intentional in the same way as human language. Some signals may be automatic responses to environmental conditions. Scientists study these behaviors to understand how communication evolved and how it supports survival.

## Questions

### 1. What is the main idea of the passage?

(A) Animals communicate only through sounds.
(B) Animal communication uses various signals and supports survival.
(C) Human language developed from bird calls.
(D) Animals never respond automatically.

### 2. Which of the following is NOT mentioned as an animal signal?

(A) Sounds
(B) Body movements
(C) Chemical substances
(D) Written symbols

### 3. Why do some birds use different calls?

(A) To identify different types of threats
(B) To attract human attention
(C) To change their environment
(D) To avoid communicating with others

### 4. What does “intentional” most nearly mean?

(A) Done on purpose
(B) Extremely loud
(C) Difficult to observe
(D) Related to movement

## Answers

1. B
2. D
3. A
4. A

## 핵심 문장

Animal communication involves different signals that can help animals survive.
